WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Let's run the actual Texas scraper kit.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:03.980
This is a recorded terminal session

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.300
using the installed product.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.060
First, the version command confirms what we're running.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.800
The environment is already set up.

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:15.353
Now we search for space exploration, limit the response to five records and save the

00:00:15.353 --> 00:00:16.253
results to a file.

00:00:17.173 --> 00:00:21.313
This command contacts the Texas Comptroller, a name match is a research lead.

00:00:21.673 --> 00:00:23.913
It does not prove that every result belongs to SpaceX.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:28.547
Next, we open the first record from the exported file.

00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:33.647
These are fields returned by the product, not example data typed into a slide.

00:00:34.247 --> 00:00:37.927
Company registration and mailing information can help your research,

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:41.007
but they don't establish ownership of a parcel near Starbase.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.783
Here's the property search help from the same installed kit.

00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:46.923
The county options are Harris and Travis.

00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:49.723
Cameron County is not supported by this command.

00:00:50.423 --> 00:00:53.343
For Starbase parcels, continue with Cameron appraisal records

00:00:53.343 --> 00:00:54.403
and county deeds.

00:00:55.043 --> 00:00:56.943
Download the free business sampler below

00:00:56.943 --> 00:00:58.623
or explore the full kit.
